wer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf3548ae-a137-5c57-8262-82ca0ade3b9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183356" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to  $x\\in N.$\n\nII. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\nIII. If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ or if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ and if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38d82c66-da81-5da6-99b2-f8009487d231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471233} {:answer/id #uuid "6cfd2ce4-c861-572f-be91-5a67f9259251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value