ur predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={Z}^{-}\\cup ∅={Z}^{-}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}={Z}^{-}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca96f6e-9734-506e-9a01-9c7094e585f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdad168-d730-54bd-a2f5-90e6a40c8c4d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd50b686-9088-5e8e-9480-616099180f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471277} {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278} :answer-field/id #uuid "185a34c6-5872-513c-806d-314d0b02664a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbc8f4a-60f3-5fff-9e49-e1ecb34e09db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471279} {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7e29fa1-6323-54f9-ac16-2c9f9af53123" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79e978ef-4c7c-5a72-a1cc-3c8d675edfbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183559" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}-2=0⇒{x}^{2}\\in N$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- **II.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$\n- **III.** $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$\\sqrt{x}-2=0$\" is the set ${4},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{2}\\in N$\" is $Z∖{0}.$\n\nSince $A⇒B≡¬A∨B,$ the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\overset{―}{{4}}\\cup (Z∖{0})=(Z∖{4})\\cup (Z∖{0})=Z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} {:answer/id #uuid "37313c70-39b7-5dc9-b3c4-a19acf370901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43f4f46-1ff7-5a5f-b67a-a7033ebb99e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca0b4c-5971-598e-b066-6bedf819e07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe01474-e943-5480-b617-9630e94ff1a0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fce173-02a3-518a-95ef-ae472714bf66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5bbf3-595e-55dd-8c22-bb49db12000e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44159662-1bf3-5bee-9ce6-75e394e9c1e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-183586" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$\n- **III.** $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all reals $x$ and $y,$ we have $\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $\\sqrt{2y}\\in R$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=-1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(x)$ is false for all values $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-1.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-2.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $y=-x$ for any value of $x.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R\\,(\\,{{∀y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ is true over the universal set $R.$ But, according to statement II, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f18e7d-fdb8-53fe-8f50-eaaac3ed1598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed5ac1a-9b04-5b9c-be9d-47fe1e8d63d8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} {:answer/id #uuid "443319b0-9a52-570e-9382-2ad4c166bcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} :answer-field/id #uuid "e823795e-dd00-51ef-b876-a9f7aa0d9ea5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbba717-65e5-566d-8fd3-783fb2ce62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471291} {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75d0c30-1919-56dd-97c7-3982426fe9c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "391922f6-f189-52a8-9bf4-83a4fbad32e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183598" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$\n- **II.** The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$\n- **III.** $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real $x$ such that, for every real $y,$ we have $xy=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $2y=0$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false.  The predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nis true for some $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,0\\cdot y=0\n$$\n\nis true. Therefore, its truth set is not empty.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R\\,(\\,{{∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a7fb68-c72a-5e28-abef-c9c14c8731f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471305} {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306} :answer-field/id #uuid "13da0634-93a4-522e-a9c5-ed03620db5cd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} {:answer/id #uuid "fd233510-4eb3-506c-8a37-8436954cbcf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b458786-6bfd-5503-9728-a374253066de" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} {:answer/id #uuid "47e244b1-8fbd-5931-8cbe-a1843732e9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fddddbd-d644-5857-bcfb-d2ac64e0c2e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e3ef236-7e81-55bf-8f08-564fa1c1ae50" :question/math-academy-id "q-183669" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}y=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,x{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,xz>3\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀$ that uses $z:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀z\\in (1,2),\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∀z}{\\overset{⏞}{x{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3}})\n$$\n\n \n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a04d1c6-5fef-5eb1-b8a0-6e8d2bc0cb0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471353} {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354} :answer-field/id #uuid "39dda0b1-b1e4-5398-90a6-9476fff2abd4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} {:answer/id #uuid "c9abd13e-9f4d-567b-bbf2-70e8c2cc7a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd300e54-475d-59cb-b72c-6f2553db14b3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} {:answer/id #uuid "e0091fd0-01af-5579-805f-bdd3dda2655a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} :answer-field/id #uuid "d218648f-439f-5a95-ad9a-80f155bba199" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a35352a2-6307-508d-9bf3-f6a84812f3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216492" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $2x+1=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- **II.** The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$\n- **III.** $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the solution of the equation $2x+1=0$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ but this solution doesn't belong to the universal set. Therefore, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement II is false.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ is empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda7182c-9b27-54fb-ae1a-8d57fe19c36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471359} {:answer/id #uuid "e32d31ef-16ba-5f7a-a9dd-81cd32b4ec01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda7182c-9b27-54fb-ae1a-8d57fe19c36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471359} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2c916d-9df2-5d54-8d54-3148860ec045" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d776f2f-d7f1-52a2-ab41-69e9765f8907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471361} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1d90a0-d385-5638-a7af-b463cfa7cd50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a1d90a0-d385-5638-a7af-b463cfa7cd50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c52a9fa8-43ce-56c3-ac5e-6c9511f4082a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24da09b9-7a22-5782-afed-5cb9868986bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471363} {:answer/id #uuid "3e03b584-5c34-5bbd-99fe-1e1d25f1324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e03b584-5c34-5bbd-99fe-1e1d25f1324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471364} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb6dd46-9d46-5c39-81ef-15638fcdf267" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "390e8909-b67e-5f3a-bb33-1726ba1d68d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-216530" :question/problem "$$\n∀{\\,y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}\\le {\\,z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $y$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+x\\le z\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $z$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $z.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\le {z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrences are \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2883b9ba-32bd-5ff5-bcce-b579c830b5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471365} {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba74c19-e05e-599b-bbd8-455461faedc0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} {:answer/id #uuid "8256ae5a-2145-576f-b24c-70fde43e43bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f394222-c342-5bf2-9565-301ff724543e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c293a14-efb0-5e66-bdb9-90ab3fd059d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471369} {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ad30a7-aa49-5946-bf6a-d22d986bc83e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d9a12d6-16ca-57db-975d-02505a889530" :question/math-academy-id "q-216618" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃z$ that uses $z:$ \n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>n+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃z}{\\overset{⏞}{{z}^{3}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $y.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in N,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} {:answer/id #uuid "191266bf-17fa-5b3f-a69d-006602f0b1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a227da-90c2-52f9-9077-b27b96efcf2d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee27b98a-d403-540e-b4d1-58599c0791ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471509} {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d0d5f5-af4c-574f-bc3d-7168cd1ab3e6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfbf44d-eb98-55d5-8c14-3e22b731f235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471511} {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e78bf6a-ca6f-5737-8263-4c7e4e4b8a4d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d63a269e-ef04-5d49-b4b0-245cf68e9dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-72167" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}.$\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $-2$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $-1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc5affe6-4770-5548-9507-5c89a64c9b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471561} {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562} :answer-field/id #uuid "320576ab-882c-5a79-b3a3-b28f006e057e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} {:answer/id #uuid "096b59d8-3cb6-5a1b-b69d-9f2da2407523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b2efca-871f-5c8a-891c-318bab239316" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b30ce9-1264-57ec-9dd7-435dcd422034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e21158-0876-5654-b53e-3a157ac915f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bf28a0-bd57-55ca-8858-3f8b81db61da" :question/math-academy-id "q-80019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}+1?$\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n- **III.** $f$ is **onto**\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/be/bed7b280998fe987276ca5820b987f672404d52d00f532db819db1166118ed70.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the lowest $y$-value is $1,$ and it occurs at the point $(2,1).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values from $y=1$ and greater, including the number $1,$ so the range of the function is $[1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Consider $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325415a9-4e64-5acc-accc-7937c4f8a651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471573} {:answer/id #uuid "509ead5d-1ed4-51e9-ade5-e20f4dccf244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509ead5d-1ed4-51e9-ade5-e20f4dccf244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471574} :answer-field/id #uuid "57e14e43-325d-539a-b71c-0daeffea3e8d" :answer-field/key "I" :a