as a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\text{Always false}}{\\overset{⏞}{P}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Statement I is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate II, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate III, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ac012a3-2b7a-5fad-8266-cc29057d1a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471411} {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412} :answer-field/id #uuid "baf6dcb7-aa48-5618-82dc-14ac46166291" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b402935f-58a9-5752-addc-960e5ce215cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471413} {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae7169b-c55d-542d-8b6e-fb38683fad9c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00902814-4c4b-5e69-95a4-aabb29cc9517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471415} {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416} :answer-field/id #uuid "847bc4cf-85e6-5570-86a1-1732fb6b1d8a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5c47e6e-a2a4-5e7d-b62c-f7e727ef436a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471417} {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f00f93a-d100-582b-98a8-1e7e4c8bdb03" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7019503-fd19-5657-a7e0-238936f56d67" :question/math-academy-id "q-334241" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the implicit Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\nI. $\\lambda Δx=0.1$\n\nII. $\\lambda Δx=0.8$\n\nIII. $\\lambda Δx=1.2$\n\nIV. $\\lambda Δx=5$\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the implicit Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method \n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the implicit Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the implicit Euler Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.1)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.1}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.1}| \\\\  & =0.9090…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.8)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.8}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.8}| \\\\  & =0.5555…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.2)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1.2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2.2}| \\\\  & =0.4545…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(5)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{6}| \\\\  & =0.1666…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV\".\n\nNote that, since the implicit Euler method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc801de-03b7-502f-b9c8-f19f4c68fc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471513} {:answer/id #uuid "d060c791-2f52-56d5-9762-68ee81769280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc801de-03b7-502f-b9c8-f19f4c68fc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471513} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd94be66-084d-5fce-b5ff-a5131094ef86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94250df-12f2-5dc7-ba7b-ba54131eb6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471515} {:answer/id #uuid "72fb50ec-bc64-58c3-b893-ff534273bff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94250df-12f2-5dc7-ba7b-ba54131eb6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471515} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6938560-02d0-5f9a-a09a-35e64a6e9bfb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371b703a-485e-500b-ad22-68bbfb32b6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471517} {:answer/id #uuid "9dadf837-5a5b-540d-9627-c3bf4d8d2d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dadf837-5a5b-540d-9627-c3bf4d8d2d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f14765-3b28-5e65-a4be-cb003368e296" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c69759b-6bd0-5ee4-a581-0fdeb88d4d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76241" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n- **I.** $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$\n- **II.** $h:[0,2\\pi ]\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(-1),$ but $1\\ne -1.$\n\n- II is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\n- III is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{{x}_{1}}) & ={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{{x}_{2}}) \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c41f62f5-7637-554e-b0a5-72527d31b936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471525} {:answer/id #uuid "4328f27e-e42d-50f8-9468-df4ad632fdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4328f27e-e42d-50f8-9468-df4ad632fdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471526} :answer-field/id #uuid "823e8dd9-ba17-5e2b-9d00-9d915e7bb0e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "544ba89c-458f-523d-9931-47036b6322fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471527} {:answer/id #uuid "842628c5-2925-52a9-b583-dda15fbe4c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "544ba89c-458f-523d-9931-47036b6322fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471527} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7f51f09-82f8-5b7d-ad8c-169eb027ae68" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e005315-61ed-5134-b31c-a6aecb8163ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471529} {:answer/id #uuid "4c22440a-ba46-5f7c-bcb0-86d279cac801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e005315-61ed-5134-b31c-a6aecb8163ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471529} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04114d1-42d1-5aca-93b9-41b8ea74c83a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03ec5353-d045-5242-94cf-0882c6a84756" :question/math-academy-id "q-77455" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n- **I.** $f:{1,2,3,4}\\to {1,2,3,4,5,6,7}$ defined by $f(x)=x+1$\n- **II.** $g:{-4,-2,0,2,4,8,10}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$\n- **III.** $h:Z\\to {-1,0,1}$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\pi )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}+1 & ={x}_{2}+1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is *not* an injection. For example, $g(-4)=16=g(4),$ but $-4\\ne 4.$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=0=h(1),$ but $0\\ne 1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70fd7763-bddf-5d4b-a0d2-d520df8819fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471531} {:answer/id #uuid "66800f24-fc8f-5965-80c0-ad7edc3f492c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70fd7763-bddf-5d4b-a0d2-d520df8819fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471531} :answer-field/id #uuid "061beb29-f49e-5ae5-80ab-2ae086130ac7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472271} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ecc4fc-b4ba-5ede-873a-b5d8fc1f5533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471533} {:answer/id #uuid "006e4f52-4ba5-5bbf-a541-0bf793ef1dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "006e4f52-4ba5-5bbf-a541-0bf793ef1dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471534} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc37ce13-8713-5918-bf02-0fc0a3a8bcfe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f520cd7-2edf-5014-99f0-3c240ef0ce88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471535} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1db73f-f393-5d05-8220-49091651b644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f520cd7-2edf-5014-99f0-3c240ef0ce88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471535} :answer-field/id #uuid "f375ed67-2bbd-5d10-83ea-65f7e6a2c2ce" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75f6f36b-64d5-52cc-809a-ed8ce71cf663" :question/math-academy-id "q-77463" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n- **I.** $f:{1,3,5,7,9}\\to {-4,-2,0,12}$ defined by $f(x)=(x-3)(x-7)$\n- **II.** $g:{1,2,3,4,5}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **III.** $h:Z\\to {-1,1}$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is *not* an injection. For example, $f(3)=0=f(7),$ but $3\\ne 7.$\n\n- II is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2),$ but $0\\ne 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b3c2fa-7551-588d-840a-ea83119bad7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471537} {:answer/id #uuid "3af9aa2b-eec1-59ce-84b4-fa541009cc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af9aa2b-eec1-59ce-84b4-fa541009cc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471538} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf6dc1f-9e90-5ea0-8430-eee9938fdcb0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "568dd441-ff12-5cb4-a941-03db3434a690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471539} {:answer/id #uuid "555408a4-81e1-5e46-9ca8-a8d529e2895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555408a4-81e1-5e46-9ca8-a8d529e2895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471540} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d798e58-7318-5c19-a372-7d8523c57d8c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83bf7342-2b6a-5899-a8fc-35881b6c4eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471541} {:answer/id #uuid "00421a0b-282f-5c80-877c-17c18d034c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83bf7342-2b6a-5899-a8fc-35881b6c4eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471541} :answer-field/id #uuid "dba742dd-43f9-5f00-ac05-4fdcec6aa9de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3065c9f8-73e6-55e4-8dcd-b18452c2889c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77465" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n- **I.** $f:{-1,0,1,2,3}\\to Z$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$\n- **II.** $g:{-2,-1,0,1,2}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={2}^{x}$\n- **III.** $h:Z\\to {-1,1}$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2),$ but $0\\ne 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bdf655b-7255-571c-b31f-2c19ac4a0867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471543} {:answer/id #uuid "dda6b314-fc5b-57b2-b98f-ffedaeec6a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bdf655b-7255-571c-b31f-2c19ac4a0867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471543} :answer-field/id #uuid "37168c2c-1edd-551c-a12f-be1dfd5b8555" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f032c94d-990d-581b-95a4-96685fcb08af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471545} {:answer/id #uuid "75eed30c-564b-56b5-8b2b-619d84b6bdba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75eed30c-564b-56b5-8b2b-619d84b6bdba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471546} :answer-field/id #uuid "993d2604-9db3-5f22-8e3f-39b362eaf4ca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c84c134-22db-5232-9a60-c3fa7e3a6d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471547} {:answer/id #uuid "d66c08b1-58cf-5699-b34c-3bb58cc74b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c84c134-22db-5232-9a60-c3fa7e3a6d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471547} :answer-field/id #uuid "99f443a7-6607-5284-b20c-ebbf85c40142" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93abda0d-dd4f-575f-bfb4-2c2551c6ca10" :question/math-academy-id "q-77821" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n- **I.** $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=|x|$\n- **II.** $g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)=4(x-2)$\n- **III.** $h:Q\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- I is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. For example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$\n\n- II is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in Q,$ we can choose an $x\\in Q$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ 4(x-2) & =y \\\\ x & =\\frac{y}{4}+2\\in Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that, \n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\frac{y}{4}+2)=4([\\frac{y}{4}+2]-2)=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ 4({x}_{1}-2) & =4({x}_{2}-2) \\\\ {x}_{1}-2 & ={x}_{2}-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- III is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$ This means that \n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nSo,  for example, there is no value $x\\in Q$ such that $h(x)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d651d58c-8505-5b88-9051-45a55fccbbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471567} {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568} :answer-field/id #uuid "104907a6-cdd1-5226-80af-9238e48719dd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} {:answer/id #uuid "c90a8158-3fa5-5544-8d1c-0590cb740f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} :answer-field/id #uuid "589fa4b5-e0cb-50a2-b3be-bd03ef21925e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} {:answer/id #uuid "83d71d17-2958-5621-b3bc-0a068a57dce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8267449-e179-58cb-88c0-3d4f6726b361" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6066c3ca-d4e8-51fc-956b-cd9926b46fbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80083" :question/problem "Let $n\\in Z.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $2$ is even, then $______.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n- **I.** $3$ is odd\n- **II.** $4$ is odd\n- **III.** $n$ is odd\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overset{\\text{Always true}}{\\overset{⏞}{Q}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Statement I is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate III, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c805415f-c87d-50c5-b668-948fc46bcc7e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e35510f-5d3e-5217-88fc-7c44b314e258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471597} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd50cb3-a32f-5f64-95e6-5ec9409e1b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfd50cb3-a32f-5f64-95e6-5ec9409e1b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471598} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d53e89a-0146-52f2-80e0-530a9e476cb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc42154a-22b3-5d68-b3c1-14f6e025d1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471599} {:answer/id #uuid "43a66160-0632-5271-b8f0-43543689ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43a66160-0632-5271-b8f0-43543689ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471600} :answer-field/id #uuid "03657d20-80fb-5db1-9d34-cc49a3cfbfe3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be073be-7f85-5018-8338-460d95a4183c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471601} {:answer/id #uuid "ed92598c-87ea-5585-b964-631e0c12952c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed92598c-87ea-5585-b964-631e0c12952c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471602} :answer-field/id #uuid "238ccfc6-a5a4-5348-aeeb-45850bb195e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4333b20-5791-5886-a0e1-73362bfffb70" :question/math-academy-id "q-80365" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3caf194f47cbc3fe36f969442df48e0a133ddbf77a9177e2e5e96822463c8a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f(0)\\ne f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is an injection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(0)=9$ (we have an arrow $0\\in X$ to $9\\in Y$) and $f(1)=0$ (we have an arrow from $1\\in X$ to $0\\in Y$).\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c805415f-c87d-50c5-b668-948fc46bcc7e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eb7ec3e-b066-53aa-967e-ca9cd6d0fe63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471603} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c2051a-3e96-5d61-baf4-fdb7c710c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0c2051a-3e96-5d61-baf4-fdb7c710c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471604} :answer-field/id #uuid "02568b8a-f1d1-5d29-922f-142e8a89353e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521299f0-65ce-5506-8da0-dc144e79a735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471605} {:answer/id #uuid "3c148df4-1f99-5d76-b25c-c53c94df0ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c148df4-1f99-5d76-b25c-c53c94df0ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471606} :answer-field/id #uuid "c006391e-2f66-5ab8-b839-5bec97c1ab80" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c7c1d5-341c-56ad-aa2e-69afee069fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471607} {:answer/id #uuid "05c53d25-667e-5047-8e41-498696abcdaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05c53d25-667e-5047-8e41-498696abcdaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471608} :answer-field/id #uuid "abdb8117-e05b-53d2-a661-ffa4d67a6d77" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf90a3c5-cc95-537c-9537-397ca87cb6b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80368" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e187742134e111e2f539fdce556c50445cc1ee8d8c6cdb93077192c14b36dfaf.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f(-5)\\ne f(0)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(-5)=3$ (we have an arrow from $-5\\in X$ to $3\\in Y$) and $f(0)=-5$ (we have an arrow from $0\\in X$ to $-5\\in Y$).\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9722747-ad43-5e96-811b-842dd883b083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471609} {:answer/id #uuid "a2947f08-7beb-5772-8a85-e8fca9381d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2947f08-7beb-5772-8a85-e8fca9381d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471610} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9c1794-b6e5-57ae-9a84-136cd5076729" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2c69ed8-da3c-55eb-8077-b33a64c36dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471611} {:answer/id #uuid "0b26bfc4-a02f-51e9-a21f-16089dcf1dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c69ed8-da3c-55eb-8077-b33a64c36dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471611} :answer-field/id #uuid "2225e57f-036f-59cf-8c55-58c73e75263b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0a05367-f30c-56a3-9601-a060c0360246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471613} {:answer/id #uuid "4675a4be-d4a9-5552-bc03-3606ccd84892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0a05367-f30c-56a3-9601-a060c0360246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471613} :answer-field/id #uuid "493ad0db-45a9-5288-b6a6-90dd145969a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0677b653-a796-5407-9e1c-60e17e55a06b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80375" :question/problem "![](images/30/309253d22ab9eaf17aeb84d504c976f0c0aeab5c8bc042f686dd69d835d53705.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(-1)=f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is an injection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the graph, we have $f(-1)=f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Again, we have $f(-1)=f(1)$ but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} {:answer/id #uuid "59363834-1ac9-5e0d-9623-b9bdf850fa57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8166f1-6fe1-57a1-9c84-1d90e80859df" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f29d7b-ddc2-512a-884a-f31bc704d36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e346a9-d793-5487-abe6-bdec0eca1c88" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} {:answer/id #uuid "691c6242-9f3b-57a5-9a92-094e02607d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd29552-cf51-56f9-888e-09e014b8609f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb0a5436-5069-574d-ac30-ea6987db593d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80376" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d81a4317d789968de29f34b42358d44e74c8bbe4717467a4c780beb633dc0d5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(-2)\\ne f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(1)=-1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(1)$ but $-2\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6537425a-3a23-527c-9da5-df969a886b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471621} {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1968b7-411d-5d23-b491-bba506874af9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620220df-3c93-5179-9f74-25ff459cd253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471623} {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa74849-6ed3-5eb6-ace4-7fa1690bd44b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36719e80-3e96-5b3d-8c80-f87abb5ce103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471625} {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b46a5ab-4a37-5bc8-a5b2-54d266daa89c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a04c07f-9732-5fba-9678-462e7c23fd4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80387" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[1,\\infty )\\to [0,\\infty )$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}?$\n- **I.** $f(1)\\ne f(2)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is **one-to-one**\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/ae/aeda30e69b9bc433e5f345822d4221e194981ce132a022f28632814376c5910e.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(1)=(1-1)^{2}=0$ and $f(2)=(2-1)^{2}=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[1,\\infty )$ that map to the same element in $[0,\\infty ).$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} {:answer/id #uuid "bed38b8f-cd64-5808-97db-78c92453dfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} :answer-field/id #uuid "12862809-b36b-5719-ad7e-aab5ef076094" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "636183c1-9b92-5010-925f-bf2aeb0bf21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471707} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96b1a9f-58a9-5646-8df6-c11742da070a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5391a9-7a0c-59b9-9fa7-c293bd935ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} :answer-field/id #uuid "f35689a1-265b-5ad7-8923-1155ca2a938d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e966053-1b79-5d5f-9b9a-6962c445b14d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82293" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd6de23e9b33d0e86a91eb4bf6b81a9d443c1b389182f1c05bf10d048f0c0402.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f$ is a surjection\n- $f$ is an injection\n- $f$ is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider $y=5.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $5\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement I is false,  $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6d0460-ea06-5cf0-9d95-66d175a22c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175