f 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471716} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd2f7d7-d32f-52ad-b157-23fafe6b4b6d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3819ae9-243b-5030-9bcc-f473557d3d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-82297" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbe19e6a595d7b48e7f18382ed0a66452ba28c86925edad81a296cb7dd26a77f.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f$ is a surjection\n- $f$ is an injection\n- $f$ is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since both statements I and II are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} {:answer/id #uuid "8322b784-b416-5f2c-bfb8-2580815fc7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca609a76-06c8-52db-8581-bd5c3848e1f6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0099d8-c719-5963-a690-03e8e902693a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c020536-4c05-52fe-a219-595565574cf0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6c6ef8-4b43-5a6a-ad55-0aa584b65ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d9db8e-6447-574c-a155-456b3f1f55a7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da5d5f20-c614-5648-b2cd-38bf72010ec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82314" :question/problem "![](images/12/126abe41ac185c082d8cc28628e2db4b2708dd84ba351718184d949ddf582d3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f$ is a surjection\n- $f$ is an injection\n- $f$ is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Consider $y=2.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $2\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement II is false. We have $f(1)=f(4)$ but $1\\ne 4.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* an injection.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement I is false (as well as statement II), $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} {:answer/id #uuid "623e141a-1cbf-55c1-8dbd-d594b76a28d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e30c4-9496-58ff-bd73-fb5da086efb0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} {:answer/id #uuid "27e78f90-3fd0-5f93-8b4a-141561c450e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdb055f-fba7-53d5-b7b3-3316bc59ab59" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} {:answer/id #uuid "195ad897-7a48-5a52-a5b1-f9353b04ade4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfaefc0f-ab90-5d24-983f-2d76b9e850dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24770296-d90b-538e-85f2-59d06d26123a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82317" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n- **I.** The function is an injection\n- **II.** The function is a surjection\n- **III.** The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. For instance, $f(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )=f(2\\pi )$, but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} {:answer/id #uuid "ad13d9ab-3383-5fe3-ad9c-1c106572bb65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc29d875-c71c-520b-b763-2a953d8a8bac" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7bbe52-574b-5d7b-b291-b264d3610735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} :answer-field/id #uuid "4693e8e4-9ee4-5e25-ba31-16678f9c6ee2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8082f6-172b-5106-960f-2a9e83d9c98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e3ba47-0ae4-55b9-8bcb-8639b038f4be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3380502f-56f6-501e-b560-ed1186ab069f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82324" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{2}-1,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n- **I.** The function is an injection\n- **II.** The function is a surjection\n- **III.** The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. For instance, $f(-1)=0=f(1)$, but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37a3a8f-ec0b-5b80-a1d8-043bba19e493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471735} {:answer/id #uuid "55b3fcf5-b4f8-5af8-80de-054df46a1c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55b3fcf5-b4f8-5af8-80de-054df46a1c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471736} :answer-field/id #uuid "d67a0411-6d24-5ee3-8f3f-ed974da2f698" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59198fa3-98de-5122-abb1-c3ee83aca1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471737} {:answer/id #uuid "56bc1bdd-021a-5112-b737-ed601332a2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59198fa3-98de-5122-abb1-c3ee83aca1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471737} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d2219b-d813-5845-84b2-eb02f91505b6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472374} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1453da03-093a-550c-8d40-7a35a58b953d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471739} {:answer/id #uuid "c9470dff-460d-54e2-b535-dd1f86b298ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1453da03-093a-550c-8d40-7a35a58b953d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471739} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fedc310-6dba-54ed-b29f-2b1a2e3131b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94a22ac-b31f-54dc-b35c-ba2dd08bc10e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82327" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef54b0fed6fa137d1a69b35c9b0231bf21192ca062fef6246df86a32591d0c0e.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={e}^{x}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- The function is an injection\n- The function is a surjection\n- The function is a bijection\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/bd/bda8097fd869dfc60ccdd2dd42d38072248ad91a94853474461d0454c30e8027.png)\n\n          \n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, ${e}^{x}>0$ for all $x\\in R.$ So, there is no value $x$ such that $f(x)=0\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f049fe-3dd5-51ea-b497-14560ab72a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471293} {:answer/id #uuid "449a440c-b8f6-5ba8-916d-314262385167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4f049fe-3dd5-51ea-b497-14560ab72a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471293} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5a451be-3277-52b0-b3b9-5ed4fa9ec66c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236782ec-1004-5c4e-b908-84cbaed85b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471295} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb6b8c1-c39b-5a07-b965-549f553c2fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "236782ec-1004-5c4e-b908-84cbaed85b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471295} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4246827-7275-54df-9a91-9ed9cd495056" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095be448-667d-5c3e-9af3-a8238f83781b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471297} {:answer/id #uuid "7c48180b-ef91-55a6-8173-f4bb51d2485b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c48180b-ef91-55a6-8173-f4bb51d2485b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471298} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7526d36-196d-56b8-94dc-a37daca6a4b7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cba8b56-135d-52f2-8f27-ede5f8ef30f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183619" :question/problem "$$\n∃{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,2-{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}={w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∃:$\n\n$$\n∃\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,2-x=w\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃x$ that uses $x:$\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃x}{\\overset{⏞}{2-{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}=w}}\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $w$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $w.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∃{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,2-{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}={w}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f71a22-fc9f-552f-a9d9-a46f8dcfc90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471299} {:answer/id #uuid "117e231e-8623-5e21-a59b-11496fbded59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f71a22-fc9f-552f-a9d9-a46f8dcfc90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471299} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c83e2c-3e5c-5076-8593-19b655c11223" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27230c26-6810-56a0-8bd7-ff8d43922f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471301} {:answer/id #uuid "114c9caf-15ed-5900-b23a-3372178c16fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "114c9caf-15ed-5900-b23a-3372178c16fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471302} :answer-field/id #uuid "6665bd07-59a9-5629-865d-a495f3ad2954" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7d0231-205c-56fd-9ea2-2ddb3e99793c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471303} {:answer/id #uuid "44987af5-9d26-5f40-b084-bcb86291212a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b7d0231-205c-56fd-9ea2-2ddb3e99793c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471303} :answer-field/id #uuid "4054af6c-64c2-5da3-8ab1-f1c077741993" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55254c80-6a13-5f2c-a4bb-f9bcddde8c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183649" :question/problem "$$\n∃\\,\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}\\,|\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $m$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∃:$\n\n$$\n∃\\,\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,n\\,|\\,m\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $m$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃m$ that uses $m:$\n\n$$\n∃\\,\\,m\\in Z,\\,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃m}{\\overset{⏞}{n\\,|\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∃\\,\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,|\\,{m}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d65819f-0528-527e-8d1a-20421e221ca5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Coterminal Angles in Radians"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feade18a-2e4c-5097-902c-711c4760cc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471377} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b889a6-9642-51fa-95e6-36a5fa1c5dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3b889a6-9642-51fa-95e6-36a5fa1c5dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471378} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b81048-0943-5c77-a333-7ca441be4347" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4a90230-6f59-512f-830c-e97128e86cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471379} {:answer/id #uuid "65dcd0b9-9263-58cd-90eb-bca20a23cfa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4a90230-6f59-512f-830c-e97128e86cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471379} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5e9d01-a48e-5e5e-8f17-d954e91b8970" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90006613-87ac-5f3e-8870-d7a821f06782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471381} {:answer/id #uuid "3013e733-3914-5bb6-86a8-a7835d0676c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3013e733-3914-5bb6-86a8-a7835d0676c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471382} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2679b75-2746-5f95-aef4-73767c3bded7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72a396d7-e8cf-5458-9d0a-c10ca03427ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-22984" :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =2\\pi $\n- **I.** $4\\pi $\n- **II.** $5\\pi $\n- **III.** $-2\\pi $\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\pi =4\\pi \\,✓$\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\cdot (2\\pi )=6\\pi $\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $6\\pi .$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\pi =0$\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-2\\pi \\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only $4\\pi $ and $-2\\pi $ are coterminal with $2\\pi .$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871d9336-19b9-50e0-bd77-0ed2445f9632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471465} {:answer/id #uuid "75776144-4d99-5b5f-b7cf-e8dd702625ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "871d9336-19b9-50e0-bd77-0ed2445f9632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471465} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d51da3-8a0a-52eb-af91-f33f62f3fbf7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dd5f287-ae86-588f-93c5-3e92c682cfc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471467} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b88c60-dc4a-5616-950a-c3e38c00242e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8b88c60-dc4a-5616-950a-c3e38c00242e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471468} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e33b7b-f740-5166-aa3a-43e201713b8e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a4d6e7e-5ad4-5acf-80a9-86cf9a9ef12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471469} {:answer/id #uuid "14887bfd-0dfd-5db8-a62b-d3da3cadabbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a4d6e7e-5ad4-5acf-80a9-86cf9a9ef12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471469} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a0e4ee-1ed3-5a2e-b4ec-e0d5e4dec86d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89b4a109-08c5-568a-830b-41c72ba008a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71401" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=1$ gives an ellipse\n- **II.** $c=2$ gives two lines\n- **III.** $c=3$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+1 & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-2){y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curve is $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which is an ellipse.\n\nSo, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c18f0539-74a8-596c-852b-0d4f3da74f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471633} {:answer/id #uuid "da87614c-db0e-5e0d-85a3-4f809e951445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c18f0539-74a8-596c-852b-0d4f3da74f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471633} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5174ed-11cb-5dac-8790-f507ecda6be1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc7392ed-77ee-5baa-b9bc-16067d951374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471635} {:answer/id #uuid "fc39236e-b074-5bb4-8887-3fc17013ce23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc39236e-b074-5bb4-8887-3fc17013ce23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471636} :answer-field/id #uuid "a26127c3-e674-5d2b-a403-9fdb7056fadf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614463b9-6217-51ba-a62e-5077088acdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471637} {:answer/id #uuid "beab60f2-37b0-54a2-8506-e97f08da4b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "614463b9-6217-51ba-a62e-5077088acdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471637} :answer-field/id #uuid "f171c56b-5039-5e7e-825f-8cf0186be360" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24df999b-6ea6-5095-ada6-d510b0d36076" :question/math-academy-id "q-80652" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n- **I.** ${f}_{x}(x,y)=4x+{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=4xy-y$\n- **II.** ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x+y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x+\\sqrt{y}$\n- **III.** ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2xy+{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}y+2x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x+{y}^{2})=2y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-y)=4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+\\sqrt{y})=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2x+2y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+2x)=2xy+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II only'."}]}
